00:00:00.196 --> 00:00:08.160
Speaker 1: Colin Powell, former secretary of&nbsp;
state, has died of COVID complications. This story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:15.760
is creating sort of an intersection of historical&nbsp;
revisionism when it comes to Colin Powell and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.600
role in foreign policy when he was secretary of&nbsp;
state. This is causing anti-vaxxers to come out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:28.800
the woodwork and say Powell was vaccinated and he&nbsp;
died, meaning the vaccine doesn't work. Why bother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.880
and get the vaccine? And it is coming at a time&nbsp;
where we are really wondering what is the future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.800
of this pandemic? So let's talk a little bit about&nbsp;
one article on this, and then we're going to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:48.320
at some clips. CNN writing Colin Powell, military&nbsp;
leader, first black U.S. secretary of state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:55.040
dies after complications from COVID 19 His&nbsp;
family announced this on Facebook. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:01.440
84. General Colin Powell, former U.S. secretary of&nbsp;
state and chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:08.320
passed away this morning due to complications from&nbsp;
COVID 19, the family wrote on Facebook, noting he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:14.080
was fully vaccinated. We have lost a remarkable&nbsp;
and loving husband, father and a great American.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.240
Um, George W. Bush said in a statement&nbsp;
today Powell was a great public servant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.640
who was such a favorite of presidents that he&nbsp;
earned the Presidential Medal of Freedom twice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.280
Highly respected home and abroad. A family man&nbsp;
and a friend. Though Powell never mounted a White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:37.520
House bid, he was sworn in as Bush's secretary of&nbsp;
state in 2001. He became the highest ranking black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.440
public official to date in the country, standing&nbsp;
forth in the presidential line of succession.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:54.960
So this is it. I won't lie and say this is not a&nbsp;
controversial figure in some sense. Colin Powell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:03.040
still haunted by Iraq and his participation&nbsp;
in making that bogus false case with nonsense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:09.840
intelligence for going into Iraq in 2003, that's&nbsp;
probably the worst of Colin Powell's legacy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.360
The good is that Colin Powell did not get pulled&nbsp;
in by the Trump cult, and even prior to that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.880
did not get pulled in by the right wing xenophobia&nbsp;
racism call when it came to President Barack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.240
Obama. So let's look at what was maybe one of&nbsp;
Colin Powell's best moments, saying, Hey, guys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.520
it's not just about whether Barack Obama is&nbsp;
a Muslim because it's being used as a slur,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:37.120
but it's also, if he were, then. So&nbsp;
what? This is maybe Powell's best moment.&nbsp;

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:43.120
Speaker 2: I'm also troubled by not what Senator&nbsp;
McCain says, but what members of the party say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.960
and it is permitted to be said such things&nbsp;
as well. You know that Mr. Obama is a Muslim.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.360
Well, the correct answer is he is not a Muslim.&nbsp;
He's a Christian. He's always been a Christian.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.560
But the really right answer is what if he is? Is&nbsp;
there something wrong with being a Muslim in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.960
country? The answer is no, that's not America.&nbsp;
Is there something wrong with some seven year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.320
old Muslim-American kid believing that he or&nbsp;
she could be president? Yet I have heard senior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:14.080
members of my own party drop the suggestion he's a&nbsp;
Muslim and he might be associated with terrorists.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.320
This is not the way we should be doing it.
Speaker 1: So that's maybe Colin Powell is best.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:26.880
Now, Colin Powell is maybe worst was participating&nbsp;
in making that case for war in Iraq based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.480
intelligence. It it seems pretty clear&nbsp;
they knew to be faulty. Take a listen.&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.680
Speaker 2: My colleagues, every statement&nbsp;
I make today is backed up by sources&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:43.840
solid sources. These are not assertions. What&nbsp;
we're giving you are facts and conclusions based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:50.320
on solid intelligence. I will cite some examples&nbsp;
and these are from human sources. Orders were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:56.240
issued to Iraq's security organizations, as well&nbsp;
as to Saddam Hussein's own office to hide all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:01.840
correspondence with the Organization of Military&nbsp;
Industrialization. This is the organization,&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:08.880
Speaker 1: and the rest, as they say, is history,&nbsp;
and that was a big factor in making the case for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:14.640
going into Iraq. One of the greatest foreign&nbsp;
policy blunders of recent decades. So a complex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:23.040
figure. And of course, we wish his family nothing&nbsp;
but the condolences and thoughts that we would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.080
when someone has lost a loved one&nbsp;
but a politically complex guy. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.840
in terms of the vaccination, there are people who&nbsp;
are going to say this and they're going to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:38.480
See why get vaccinated? Colin Powell was fully&nbsp;
vaccinated and he still died from complications&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:44.640
from COVID. Remember, Colin Powell was 84 years&nbsp;
old. Very, very high risk group. As we know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:52.160
no vaccine is 100 percent. And we have seen a very&nbsp;
small number proportionally, but we have seen some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:59.920
so-called breakthrough deaths. What we should be&nbsp;
saying in reaction to this is wow. It is way more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:05.920
common to die when you're not vaccinated at any&nbsp;
age. I should get vaccinated. You look at public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.080
hospitalization data. We just got some recent&nbsp;
data from the UK, which is why I mention it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:18.400
84 percent of hospitalizations in the UK&nbsp;
were unvaccinated. Only half of one percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:26.480
of COVID deaths in the UK were fully vaccinated.&nbsp;
And so while this does happen statistically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:32.240
and it just so happens that Colin Powell is now&nbsp;
one of those in that group, you are overwhelmingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.840
protected from hospitalization and from death if&nbsp;
you get vaccinated. So the message should be, wow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:44.400
it's newsworthy because it is so rare&nbsp;
statistically that fully vaccinated people die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:51.200
This really reinforces the importance of the&nbsp;
vaccine. So that is that's the mathematically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:58.880
